# uninit_10: ANCHOR -- the prior use is a freed HEAP CHUNK out of the tcache.
#
# Protections for the uninitialised-memory-disclosure (CWE-457/CWE-908) variant
# corpus. Held IDENTICAL across all six targets on purpose: WHICH PRIOR USE OF
# THE RECORD'S BYTES SURVIVES INTO THE DISCLOSED TAIL is the only variable, so a
# protection difference would confound the measurement.
#
# -fstack-protector-all  ON, and load-bearing twice over. (a) The category is
#                        orthogonal to the canary -- nothing here overflows --
#                        so the strongest stack hardening being on is the point
#                        rather than an oversight. (b) uninit_13's axis point IS
#                        the canary: its disclosure window covers a returned
#                        deeper frame's canary slot, so the canary has to exist
#                        for that point on the axis to exist at all. `-all`
#                        rather than `-strong` so every function in the family
#                        stores it, which is what makes the slot's position a
#                        property of the frame layout instead of a gcc heuristic.
# -no-pie                uninit_13 finishes with ret2win, and this family
#                        forbids the code-pointer resolve chain that a PIE image
#                        would need (see corpus_uninit.yaml, "DELIBERATELY NOT
#                        COVERED"). -no-pie is the one deliberate weakening and
#                        it is held across all six so it cannot confound.
# -Wl,-z,relro,-z,now    FULL RELRO. Nothing in this family writes a GOT entry,
#                        so the strictest setting costs nothing and removes any
#                        question of a solve having gone through the GOT.
# -O0                    the whole category depends on the compiler NOT
#                        initialising what the source leaves alone. At higher -O
#                        gcc is free to fold the partially-written record into
#                        registers, to sink the `write` before the `read`, or to
#                        drop the unused 256-byte `arg` that this family's stack
#                        geometry depends on -- any of which silently stops the
#                        target being in this category.
#
# NOT SET, and stated rather than left to inference: no -fno-stack-protector
# anywhere (contrast benchmark/corpus_bon), and no -z execstack. NX is on by
# gcc's default here and is MEASURED off the binaries in corpus_uninit.yaml
# rather than assumed from these flags.
-fstack-protector-all
-no-pie
-Wl,-z,relro,-z,now
-O0
